  "whep_failure_diagnosis": {
    "symptom": "31 Oct 2026: WHEP unavailable, written 3 dropped 434. Reproduced in the live session of 7 Nov (job 3): written 3, dropped 2002, error '[Errno 32] Broken pipe', /media/whep 404.",
    "root_cause": "The simulation is synchronous and publishes no frame while the model thinks or the session waits (startup, model load, waiting for pairing). MediaMTX's default RTSP read timeout is 10 s: it closed the ffmpeg publisher ('i/o timeout' in mediamtx.log 10 s after the first burst), ffmpeg's tee muxer aborted with a broken pipe, MediaRuntime recorded the error and never restarted the encoder, so 'available' stayed false and every later frame was dropped. Not the NVENC encoder and not IAP.",
    "isolated_without_simulator": "probe job 2 (stall_then_resume: 5 frames, 15 s silence, 50 frames): written 6, dropped 47, error Broken pipe; the steady 10 Hz scenario was fine (300/300).",
    "fix": "media_config readTimeout 3600 s (commit 5ee19d2). Verified: probe job 4 stall_then_resume 55/55 written, 0 dropped; live job 5 written == submitted (602/602) with no error across model-inference pauses; job 6 see vm_side."
  },
