  "bottleneck": {
    "iap_connection_setup": "A new TCP connection through IAP costs about 1 s (no keep-alive GET /status median in api_rtt_new_connection_ms) whereas a kept-alive connection round-trips in roughly 115-140 ms. A client that opened a new connection per frame would be limited to about 1 frame/s; the web client's long-lived stream and keep-alive avoid that.",
    "delivered_fps": "Delivered rate follows the simulator's frame production while a task runs (a few frames per second with pauses during Qwen inference), not IAP: push delivered every sequence number (sequence_frames_never_shown 0) while polling skipped frames it could not request in time.",
    "verdict": "No JPEG transport over IAP was found to be the limit at the simulator's rate. WHEP over ICE/TCP through IAP works after the MediaMTX fix but showed freezes, 0.4-0.56 s jitter-buffer delay and dropped frames (see whep_over_iap_tcp); its source-to-screen latency was not measurable."
  },
  "status": "PARTIAL: fps, JPEG capture-to-screen latency, loss, reconnect and fallback measured; WHEP latency not measured; Tailnet skipped.",
